      "title": "Multimodal Models: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Multimodal Models: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The VLM Idea",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==VLM==: image + text in, **text** out",
                "Image becomes embeddings the LLM reads like {blue:extra tokens}",
                "Three parts: ==vision encoder== (usually a ViT), ==projector==, ==LLM decoder==",
                "Projector: linear layer or MLP, sometimes cross-attention"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Vision encoder",
                    "sub": "ViT",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Projector",
                    "sub": "linear / MLP",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "LLM decoder",
                    "sub": "text out",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Fusion Styles",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Early fusion",
                "Cross-attention"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Example",
                  "LLaVA",
                  "Flamingo"
                ],
                [
                  "Image tokens",
                  "Join the LLM sequence",
                  "Kept separate, attended across"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. One Shared Space",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Modality",
                "Pipeline"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Image",
                  "patches → embeddings"
                ],
                [
                  "Audio",
                  "spectrogram → embeddings"
                ],
                [
                  "Text",
                  "subword tokens → embeddings"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Projector",
              "text": "It maps vision features into the ==LLM embedding dimension==, so image vectors fit the decoder."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Three VLM parts?** Vision encoder, projector, LLM decoder",
                "**Early vs cross-attention?** Tokens join the sequence vs separate streams attended across",
                "**Why project?** Vision features must match the LLM embedding dimension"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Image Tokens, Patches and Contrastive Training",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Image Tokens, Patches and Contrastive Training",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Patches Become Tokens",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Split",
                    "sub": "fixed 16x16 patches",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Flatten",
                    "sub": "pixels to vector",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Project",
                    "sub": "linear layer",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Add position",
                    "sub": "embeddings",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each patch = ==one image token==",
                "Tokens = (H/P) x (W/P)",
                "Double the resolution: ==4x tokens== and far more attention cost"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Image",
                "Patch",
                "Grid",
                "Tokens"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "224x224",
                  "16x16",
                  "14x14",
                  "196"
                ],
                [
                  "336x336",
                  "14x14",
                  "24x24",
                  "576"
                ],
                [
                  "448x448",
                  "16x16",
                  "28x28",
                  "784"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. CLIP Contrastive Loss",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Image and text encoders trained ==jointly== on image-caption pairs",
                "Matching pairs get high ==cosine similarity== in a shared space",
                "Batch of N: N diagonal {green:positives}, N²-N {red:negatives}",
                "==Symmetric cross-entropy== over rows and columns",
                "A learned ==temperature== scales the logits",
                "Bigger batch = more negatives = better training"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Zero-Shot Classification",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Embed `a photo of a {class}` for every class",
                "Embed the image",
                "Pick the ==highest cosine similarity=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**336x336 with 14x14 patches?** 24 x 24 = ==576 tokens==",
                "**Why large batches?** More negatives per positive pair",
                "**Zero-shot?** Class prompts vs image embedding, take max cosine"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Diffusion Basics for Image Generation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Diffusion Basics for Image Generation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Forward and Reverse",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Clean image",
                    "sub": "x0",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Add Gaussian noise",
                    "sub": "T steps",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pure noise",
                    "sub": "xT",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Learned denoiser",
                    "sub": "step by step",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{orange:Forward}: add ==Gaussian noise== over **T steps** until pure noise",
                "{blue:Reverse}: a ==learned denoiser== removes noise step by step",
                "Train: random timestep `t`, noise a clean image, **predict the added noise**",
                "Loss = ==MSE== between predicted and true noise; net is a U-Net or transformer"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Latent Diffusion",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Runs in a compressed ==VAE latent space==, not pixel space",
                "Far **cheaper** than pixel diffusion (Stable Diffusion)",
                "The ==VAE decoder== turns the final latent into an image"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Conditioning and Sampling",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Text encoder (**CLIP** or **T5**) feeds ==cross-attention== in the denoiser",
                "==Classifier-free guidance== blends conditional and unconditional predictions"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Knob",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Guidance scale up",
                  "closer to prompt, {red:less diversity}, possible oversaturation"
                ],
                [
                  "Fewer steps (20-30, DPM++ / Euler)",
                  "{green:faster}, lower quality"
                ],
                [
                  "Same seed",
                  "same starting noise, reproducible output"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "What does the denoiser predict in training? **The added noise.** Why latent space? **Far cheaper.** What does guidance scale control? **Prompt adherence vs diversity.**"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
